# Week 1 — Initial Discovery

## 1. Facts
People sign up using emails, phone calls, paper forms, or spreadsheets instead of one central place
Event organisers spend hours matching the right volunteers to the right tasks by hand
Volunteers often do not know which events actually need help
is hard to let everyone know quickly when an event schedule changes or gets cancelled
Some tasks need specific skills, background checks, or qualifications

## 2. Assumptions
Organisers have internet access during operational hours
Volunteers prefer updates by text or email instead of phone calls
Each event has a maximum number of volunteers it can accept


## 3. Unknowns
How are volunteer qualifications and background checks currently verified
Who has authority to create, modify, or cancel a community event
What privacy restrictions apply to sharing volunteer contact details

## 4. Stakeholders
Event organiser: needs easy matching tools. Concerned about last-minute cancellations
General volunteer: needs clear schedule visibility. Concerned about missing updates
Skilled volunteer: needs role-specific assignments matching qualifications
IT support: needs security and account management
Privacy officer: needs compliance with data protection laws
Community members: needs clear, timely event information and accessible support. Concern about unreliable communication, missed events or poor support quality
Sponsors: needs Simple reports showing community impact and how funds are used. Concern about Lack of transparency or wasted funding

